# Silver Traverse V1.3 — Hedonic-Rebase Blinded Validation Plan

**Formula:** `SILVER_TRAVERSE_V1_3_30mL_20pct_THEORY.md`  
**Protocol ID:** ST-V1.3-HR-BLIND-20260828  
**Exact predecessor controls:** V1.2 formula and V1.2 blind plan, preserved unchanged  
**Status:** THEORY PROTOCOL ONLY / NOT RUN / NO COMPOUNDING OR PROCUREMENT AUTHORIZED  
**Claim ceiling:** this design cannot establish Pink Pepper identity/equivalence, hedonism, liking, comfort, luxury, depth, completion, safety, stability, diffusion, or longevity until separately authorized blinded physical observations exist

## Purpose and Decision Order

The protocol separates three questions that theory cannot answer:

1. Does the CURRENT four-function reconstruction form one integrated Pink-Pepper-like subject rather than Black Pepper plus rose?
2. Do reduced upper glare and softened rear pressure improve liking and re-smell desire while preserving identity?
3. On the surviving dose architecture, is Habanolide more hedonic and target-exact than Romandolide, Ethylene Brassylate, or no musk?

Run stages in this order:

1. protected identity and takeover gate;
2. glare-relief (`G`) x softened-pressure/release (`S`) 2 x 2 with Romandolide held fixed;
3. one-musk tournament on the selected dose architecture;
4. direct V1.2-versus-V1.3 confirmation in fresh independent blocks;
5. citrus refinement and low-OAV structural omissions;
6. 36-row versus 31-row compression and isolated add-backs.

No later liking result rescues a failure of the protected Pink Pepper identity or a repeated takeover exclusion.

## Preconditions for Any Future Physical Work

All applicable boxes require separate authorization before preparation:

- [ ] AGENTS, live inventory, Copilot instructions, family reference, current DHP protocol, studio method, V1.1/V1.2/V1.3 formulas, and all linked blind plans re-read for that physical batch
- [ ] formula/source hashes and exact stock/container IDs recorded
- [ ] Pink Pepper ownership status reconfirmed; no purchase inferred from this protocol
- [ ] Black Pepper, Rose Oxide, Damascone Beta, Geraniol, Bergamot, Cedrat, BONTAUX lavender, vetiver, patchouli, Labdanum, and all musk bottle identities/condition recorded
- [ ] natural-mixture composite coverage and canonical aliases checked; missing coverage stays HOLD
- [ ] current Ambrox w/v basis accepted for exploratory use or reconciled
- [ ] Peppermint 10% w/w DPG working stock separately authorized, prepared from a raw aliquot of at least 10 uL, labeled, and recorded
- [ ] formula-specific IFRA/allergen and material-safety review completed
- [ ] blotter work separately authorized; skin work remains separately gated
- [ ] two independent preparation blocks, concealed code key, evaluator/preparer roles, and balanced order assigned

Any unresolved applicable precondition leaves the run on **HOLD**.

## General Controls

- Every arm is raw-volume constant at 6,000 uL concentrate. Active mass is not necessarily constant because stock strengths differ; record the limitation.
- Benzyl Benzoate is the declared low-character compensator and negative-space owner. It is not proven neutral. If evaluators detect it as the causal difference, the affected comparison is **HOLD / RE-DESIGN**.
- No direct raw or working-stock aliquot may be below 10 uL.
- Use two independently rebuilt blocks. Duplicate strips from one master assess read consistency, not independent preparation.
- Use nonsemantic random codes, conceal the key until data lock, and balance serving order across sessions/assessors.
- Record free description and first named object before revealing the perfume name or anchored prompts.
- Blotter reads: 0, 5, 30, and 120 minutes; 6 and 24 hours. Skin remains HOLD pending separate safety authority.
- Identity, liking, desire to re-smell, comfort, intensity, harshness, fatigue, and depth are separate endpoints.

## Stage 0A — CURRENT Reconstruction: Spicy Pressure x Rosy Facets

Geraniol 10% at 30 uL remains common as the seam into lavender. All unshown rows remain at V1.3 doses.

| Arm | Black Pepper EO | Rose Oxide 1% | Damascone Beta 10% | Benzyl Benzoate | Total |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| P+R+ | 180 | 20 | 10 | 330 | 6,000 |
| P+R- | 180 | 0 | 0 | 360 | 6,000 |
| P-R+ | 0 | 20 | 10 | 510 | 6,000 |
| P-R- | 0 | 0 | 0 | 540 | 6,000 |

Record first object; Pink-Pepper fit; rosy, berry-bright, effervescent, woody-spicy, hot/dry, culinary, metallic, lychee, plum, and literal-rose cues; integration versus fragmentation; lead rank through 120 minutes; and recurrence at 6/24 hours.

For each endpoint within each independent block:

```text
P main effect = ((P+R- + P+R+) - (P-R- + P-R+)) / 2
R main effect = ((P-R+ + P+R+) - (P-R- + P+R-)) / 2
P x R interaction = P+R+ - P+R- - P-R+ + P-R-
```

The full reconstruction survives only if the interaction repeatedly creates one integrated rosy-effervescent pepper subject and preserves Silver Traverse identity without more hot/dry pepper, literal rose/plum, harshness, fatigue, or fragmentation. A liked but non-Pink-Pepper-like arm fails the protected criterion.

### Stage 0B — Pepper-pressure rescue

Run only if Black Pepper contributes identity but 180 uL is too hot, dry, or tiring.

| Arm | Black Pepper EO | Rose Oxide 1% | Damascone Beta 10% | Benzyl Benzoate | Total |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| P180 | 180 | 20 | 10 | 330 | 6,000 |
| P090 | 90 | 20 | 10 | 420 | 6,000 |
| P000 | 0 | 20 | 10 | 510 | 6,000 |

Prefer the lowest dose that preserves integrated rosy-spice identity and recurrence with less heat/fatigue.

### Stage 0C — Damascone necessity

- `D+`: Damascone Beta 10% 10 uL; Benzyl Benzoate 330 uL.
- `D-`: Damascone Beta 0; Benzyl Benzoate 340 uL.

Retain Damascone only if it repeatedly creates a later berry-woody recollection of the opening without becoming rose/plum-like. “Richer” alone is insufficient.

### Stage 0D — Contingent exact Pink Pepper comparison

This stage is contingent on later, separately authorized access to a documented exact Pink Pepper EO. It does not authorize procurement.

Build a 5,520 uL common background from V1.3 by removing Black Pepper 180, Rose Oxide 20, Damascone Beta 10, and 270 uL of the 330 uL Benzyl Benzoate row. The common background retains Benzyl Benzoate 60 uL and Geraniol 10% 30 uL.

| Arm | 480 uL identity module | Interpretation |
|---|---|---|
| E480 | exact Pink Pepper EO 480 uL | TARGET hero at 80,000 ppm |
| R480 | Black Pepper 180 + Rose Oxide 1% 20 + Damascone Beta 10% 10 + Benzyl Benzoate 270 | CURRENT reconstruction |
| N480 | Benzyl Benzoate 480 | no pepper-subject control |

Exact Pink Pepper identity is supported only if coded free descriptions repeatedly recover the intended rosy-effervescent subject in E480 with better integration and lead persistence and no new safety/takeover failure. R480 cannot be called chemically or sensorially equivalent merely because it is preferred.

## Stage 1 — Glare Relief x Softened Pressure/Release 2 x 2

Hold Romandolide at 250 uL in all four arms so musk character cannot confound the dose-architecture test. The `00` arm is exact V1.2; `11` is the V1.3 dose rebase with Romandolide in place of Habanolide.

### G factor — upper-glare relief with declared negative space

| Row | G- raw uL | G+ raw uL | Delta |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Cedrat | 40 | 20 | -20 |
| Bergamot | 80 | 40 | -40 |
| Dihydromyrcenol | 100 | 60 | -40 |
| Linalyl Acetate | 200 | 180 | -20 |
| BONTAUX Lavender | 300 | 240 | -60 |
| Clary Sage | 80 | 60 | -20 |
| Cyclamen Aldehyde | 50 | 20 | -30 |
| Benzyl Benzoate | 100 | 330 | +230 |
| **NET** |  |  | **0** |

### S factor — rear-pressure reallocation into release/cushion

| Row | S- raw uL | S+ raw uL | Delta |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Iso E Super | 800 | 770 | -30 |
| Ambrox Super nominal 33% | 950 | 920 | -30 |
| Clearwood | 270 | 270 | 0 |
| Azarbre | 300 | 300 | 0 |
| Timberol | 120 | 100 | -20 |
| Ambermax 50% | 100 | 70 | -30 |
| Hedione | 580 | 600 | +20 |
| Helional | 80 | 100 | +20 |
| Dihydrojasmone | 50 | 70 | +20 |
| Hexyl Salicylate | 250 | 300 | +50 |
| **NET** |  |  | **0** |

| Arm | G | S | Romandolide | Total | Causal question |
|---|---|---|---:|---:|---|
| 00 | V1.2 glare | V1.2 rear pressure | 250 | 6,000 | exact predecessor |
| 10 | relieved | V1.2 rear pressure | 250 | 6,000 | does subtraction/negative space improve identity and ease? |
| 01 | V1.2 glare | softened/released | 250 | 6,000 | does pressure reallocation create deeper, more yielding structure? |
| 11 | relieved | softened/released | 250 | 6,000 | V1.3 dose architecture before musk choice |

For each governed endpoint:

```text
G main effect = ((10 + 11) - (00 + 01)) / 2
S main effect = ((01 + 11) - (00 + 10)) / 2
G x S interaction = 11 - 10 - 01 + 00
```

The `11` architecture survives only if it preserves first-object Pink Pepper fit and late base identity while improving repeated liking or re-smell desire beyond the additive expectation, without higher blandness, compensator detection, harshness, fatigue, muddiness, generic freshness, or loss of technical tension. A quieter arm is not automatically more hedonic or deeper.

## Stage 2 — Single-Musk Tournament

Run on the dose architecture selected in Stage 1. The table below assumes `11`; if another architecture wins, retain its actual Benzyl Benzoate dose and apply the same equal-volume substitutions.

| Arm | Sole musk | Musk uL | Benzyl Benzoate | Total | Exact hypothesis |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| R | Romandolide | 250 | 330 | outward woody-clean technical-fabric halo |
| H | Habanolide | 250 | 330 | inward skin-comfort veil; V1.3 candidate |
| E | Ethylene Brassylate | 250 | 330 | creamy/lactonic skin depth; takeover-risk comparator |
| N | none | 0 | 580 | no-musk clarity control |

Do not combine candidate musks. Evaluate outward halo, inward comfort, cream/lactone, powder, laundry, masking, skin/fabric identity, lead persistence, liking, and re-smell desire separately.

Habanolide is selected only if H repeatedly improves comfort and liking while preserving Pink Pepper leadership, technical textile identity, and recurrence better than R, E, and N. Romandolide wins if outward motion is more target-exact and equally or more liked. EB wins only if its creamy depth is target-linked rather than merely smooth. N wins if every musk masks or genericizes the composition. Ambrettolide is reserved for a later separately designed arm only if all four fail and a specific fruity-naturalistic skin deficit is observed.

## Stage 3 — Fresh-Block Predecessor Confirmation

After Stages 0-2 choose an eligible V1.3 branch, compare in two newly prepared independent blocks:

- `P`: exact V1.2 formula at 6,000 uL.
- `S`: selected V1.3 branch at 6,000 uL.

This comparison confirms the combined successor but cannot localize causality; localization comes from Stages 1 and 2. V1.3 is preferred only if S preserves the protected identity and improves liking or desire to re-smell without more takeover, harshness, fatigue, muddiness, or loss of spatial/temporal structure in both blocks.

## Stage 4 — Citrus Refinement and Structural Omissions

### Stage 4A — citrus full/half/zero

All other selected rows remain fixed.

| Arm | Bergamot | Cedrat | Benzyl Benzoate versus selected V1.3 | Total |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| C60 | 40 | 20 | 330 | 6,000 |
| C30 | 20 | 10 | 360 | 6,000 |
| C00 | 0 | 0 | 390 | 6,000 |

Choose the lowest dose that adds floral-bitter peel dimension, pepper legibility, and transition without taking first-object leadership. Cedrat 10 uL in C30 exactly meets the direct floor.

### Stage 4B — Hexyl Salicylate structural necessity

- `X+`: Hexyl Salicylate 300 uL; Benzyl Benzoate at the selected dose.
- `X-`: Hexyl Salicylate 0; Benzyl Benzoate +300 uL.

Retain Hexyl Salicylate only if dry-cloth cushion, continuity, or pressure release is repeatedly lost on omission. Modeled OAV below 1 cannot establish that function.

### Stage 4C — far-rear Labdanum shadow

- `L+`: Labdanum Resinoid 10% 100 uL; selected Benzyl Benzoate dose.
- `L-`: Labdanum 0; Benzyl Benzoate +100 uL.

Retain only if a distinct far-rear shadow and named base identity improve without sweetness, smoke, leather, or detected compensator confounding.

## Stage 5 — 36 Rows versus 31 Rows

The compressed arm removes five finishing hypotheses and moves their 290 uL raw total to Benzyl Benzoate.

| Removed row | Raw uL | Predicted loss if useful |
|---|---:|---|
| Methyl Pamplemousse 10% | 40 | weaker grapefruit-peel spark and pepper-to-vetiver recurrence |
| Terpinyl Acetate | 30 | weaker pine-citrus stitch into lavender |
| Dihydrojasmone | 70 | less dry moving-fabric release |
| Labdanum Resinoid 10% | 100 | flatter far-rear shadow |
| Vetival | 50 | rougher, less polished vetiver echo |
| **Total to Benzyl Benzoate** | **290** |  |

For the V1.3 Habanolide candidate, Benzyl Benzoate becomes 620 uL in the 31-row arm. If an earlier stage selects another branch, add 290 uL to that branch's actual compensator dose. Hide ingredient count from evaluators.

Prefer 31 rows if it equals or improves Pink Pepper leadership, name identity, states, planes, recurrence, liking, fatigue, and takeover profile. The 36-row arm survives only if its repeatable advantage is localized to a predicted loss. “Richer,” “more complex,” or “more expensive-smelling” is insufficient.

### Stage 5B — isolated add-backs

Run only if 36 rows beats 31. Starting from the selected compressed arm, add one row and remove the same raw volume from Benzyl Benzoate:

| Arm | Add-back | Benzyl Benzoate decrement |
|---|---|---:|
| M | Methyl Pamplemousse 10% 40 uL | -40 |
| T | Terpinyl Acetate 30 uL | -30 |
| D | Dihydrojasmone 70 uL | -70 |
| L | Labdanum Resinoid 10% 100 uL | -100 |
| V | Vetival 50 uL | -50 |

Retain only rows whose observed change matches the pre-declared prediction in both blocks without drift, harshness, muddiness, fatigue, or compensator detection.

